  "query_preview": "..\n\nToday through Wednesday...\n\nA cold front moves through the region this morning, bringing\nwidespread breezy winds out of the northwest in the 40s and 50s\nmph and much cooler temperatures. Highs will be in the 40s to low\n50s today, ranging from 20 to nearly 40 degrees cooler than \nWednesday.\n\nA wave of precipitation will accompany the front, bringing a\nwidespread 60-80% chance of precip through the morning hours.\nThrough the rest of today into Friday, the upper low to the\nnortheast will continue to wrap around precip, favoring the\nmountains and foothills. Over the mountains, precip will fall as\nsnow, with expected 10-18 inches over the Beartooth/Absaroka and \nCrazy mountains and 6-12 inches over the Bighorn mountains through\nFriday night. Lower elevations will see rain to start, with the \nfoothills switching over to mostly snow as the front moves through\nand the plains switching to snow Thursday evening as temps drop \nbelow freezing. Over the Beartooth foothills, expect to see 2-5 \ninches of snow through Friday night. Outside of the foothills, \nlittle to no snow accumulations are expected, with generally a \nless than 15% chance of at least an inch of snow.\n\nHighs Friday will be generally in the 40s. The weekend into early\nnext week will remain unsettled, with daily 30-50% chances for\nlight snow and rain/snow showers. Highs will be warming towards \nnormal for this time of year (upper 50s to low 60s) by Tuesday.\nArcher",
